$\n\n \n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=0$ and $x=2.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-1,1,3$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =(-1)^{3}(-1-2)=3>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =(1)^{3}(1-2)=-1<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =(3)^{3}(3-2)=27>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $0$ | $(0,2)$ | $2$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-1$ |  | $1$ |  | $3$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |\n\nSo, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534541 true] [17592186293877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293878 13194139534541 true] [17592186293877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293879 13194139534541 true] [17592186293877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293880 13194139534541 true] [17592186293877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293881 13194139534541 true] [17592186293877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293882 13194139534541 true] [17592186293877 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534541 true] [17592186293877 1041 "selection" 13194139534541 true] [17592186293877 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293880 13194139534541 true] [17592186293877 1110 #uuid "0d34f65d-1c29-54b6-987f-68e2c7328b04" 13194139534541 true] [17592186293878 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534541 true] [17592186293878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534541 true] [17592186293878 1111 #uuid "cc367a49-bbe1-53b2-b92f-9665a6e0a876" 13194139534541 true] [17592186293879 1034 "I only" 13194139534541 true] [17592186293879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534541 true] [17592186293879 1111 #uuid "de10b173-78aa-5bb6-8877-3b9e366c4ae0" 13194139534541 true] [17592186293880 1034 "III only" 13194139534541 true] [17592186293880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534541 true] [17592186293880 1111 #uuid "3df